==Galician==

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|gl|ile|il}}
* {{alt|gl|ele||reintegrationist}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|gl|la|ille||that}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|gl|/ˈel/}}
* {{rhymes|gl|el}}
* {{hyphenation|gl|el}}

===Pronoun===
{{gl-pron|g=m|dat=lle|acc=o}}

# [[he]]
# [[it]] {{gloss|impersonal pronoun, optative subject of impersonal verbs}}
#: {{uxi|gl|'''El''' chove|'''It''' rains}}
# [[it]] {{gloss|optatively, can introduce a question}}
#: {{uxi|gl|Que cousa preciosa! '''El''' será pecado?|What a precious thing! Could '''it''' be a sin?}}

====Usage notes====
The accusative form {{m|gl|o}} has variant forms {{m|gl|lo}} and {{m|gl|no}}. These alternative forms appear depending on the ending of the preceding word. The form {{m|gl||lo}} is used when the preceding word ends in {{m|gl||-r}} or {{m|gl||-s}}. The {{m|gl||no}} form is used when the preceding word ends in {{m|gl||-u}} or a diphthong. These alternative forms are then suffixed to the preceding word.

The accusative also forms contractions when it immediately follows an indirect object pronoun. For example, {{m|gl||dou che o}} contracts to {{m|gl||doucho|I gave it to you}}.

