=====Usage notes=====
* The prepositions {{m|es|de}} and {{m|es|a}} contract with {{m|es||el}}, unless {{m|es||el}} is part of a proper noun.
*: {{ux|es|El libro '''del''' niño me enseñó sobre la oscilación '''de El''' Niño.|'''The''' boy''''s''' book taught me about the oscillation '''of El''' Niño.}}
*: {{ux|es|Fuimos '''a El''' Salvador y le rezamos '''al''' Salvador.|We went '''to El''' Salvador and prayed '''to the''' Savior.}}
* Spanish definite articles are used in some contexts where English uses possessive pronouns.
*: {{ux|es|Tengo '''las''' manos sucias.|'''My''' hands are dirty.}}
*: {{ux|es|Me duele '''la''' pierna.|'''My''' leg hurts.}}
* Spanish definite articles are used when talking about a whole group in general or abstract notions, unlike English ones.
*: {{ux|es|'''Los''' guepardos son el animal terreste más veloz.| Cheetahs are the fastest land animal.}}
*: {{ux|es|'''El''' amor es siempre paciente y amable.| Love is always patient and kind.}}

